<section id="problem" class="studio-problem reference-section" data-tone="light"><div class="wrap studio-two"><div><span class="eyebrow">DATASET SHORTCUTS</span><h2 class="reading-statement" data-reading>Models can learn dataset cues</h2><p class="statement-answer">When a dataset mostly contains one joint, a model can use cues such as framing or image dimensions to guess the joint. Compare predictions from checkpoints trained with and without FracAtlas.</p></div><div class="pixel-specimen"><img src="{{sample_file}}" alt="FracAtlas radiograph from specimen {{sample_number}}" width="{{sample_width}}" height="{{sample_height}}" loading="lazy"><span class="spec-tag tag-one">Pooled · {{prediction}}</span><span class="spec-tag tag-two">No FracAtlas · {{shift_prediction}}</span><span class="spec-tag tag-three">Confidence ≠ correctness</span><span class="pixel-caption">ONE IMAGE. DIFFERENT TRAINING.</span></div></div></section>
<section id="benchmark-checkpoints" class="decision-section reference-section" data-tone="volt"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">THREE-CLASS BENCHMARK</span><div class="decision-heading"><h2>Four training sets,<br><em>one radiograph</em></h2><div class="confidence-hero"><b>{{confidence}}<span>%</span></b><p>pooled softmax score<br>for this sample’s predicted joint.</p></div></div><div class="decision-cards"><article class="primary-receipt"><header><span class="receipt-code">E0</span><div><h3>Pooled checkpoint</h3><p>EfficientNet-B3 · all six sources · seed 0</p></div><span class="best-badge">SAME IMAGE</span></header><div class="receipt-spec"><img src="{{sample_file}}" alt="FracAtlas radiograph from specimen {{sample_number}}" width="{{sample_width}}" height="{{sample_height}}"><div><span>SPECIMEN {{sample_number}} · FRACATLAS</span><strong>{{prediction}}</strong><p>{{confidence}}% softmax confidence</p></div></div><div class="receipt-breakdown"><div><span>Input</span><b>Greyscale · 160 × 160</b></div><div><span>Task</span><b>Hip / Knee / Shoulder</b></div><div><span>Activation view</span><b>Pooled-model Grad-CAM</b></div><div><span>Data handling</span><b>In memory · no image storage</b></div></div><a href="demo.html?sample={{sample_number}}">Run this specimen in the workbench →</a><p class="receipt-caveat">{{sample_note}}</p></article><div class="other-receipts">{{checkpoint_receipts}}<div class="why-card"><span>WHY FOUR CHECKPOINTS?</span><p>The input stays the same. The training sources change. Compare the effect directly.</p></div></div></div></div></section>
