<section id="workflow" class="workflow-section reference-section" data-tone="dark"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">X-RAY WORKFLOW</span><div class="workflow-layout"><div><h2>From X-ray upload<br><em>to review report</em></h2><p>Upload an X-ray or choose a sample. The workbench shows the expanded anatomy scores, four benchmark predictions and a Grad-CAM overlay.</p><div class="pipeline-states"><span>IMAGE SELECTED</span><span>VALIDATED</span><span>PREPROCESSED</span><span class="state-active">INFERENCE</span><span>COMPARED</span><span>VISUALIZED</span></div><a href="methodology.html">Read the methods →</a></div><div class="workflow-card"><header><span class="state-dot"></span><b>Inference steps</b></header><ol><li><span>01</span><div><b>Select or upload</b><p>JPEG, PNG, BMP, WebP or TIFF · up to 12 MB.</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><b>Prepare the input</b><p>Greyscale, 160 px and the recorded normalization.</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><b>Run the checkpoints</b><p>One six-region model and four benchmark checkpoints run locally on CPU.</p></div></li><li><span>04</span><div><b>Review the predictions</b><p>Region scores and cutoffs, benchmark agreement, and the pooled checkpoint’s Grad-CAM overlay.</p></div></li></ol><div class="workflow-callout"><span>INPUT STAYS THE SAME</span><p>The checkpoints differ in their training sources. The report compares their joint predictions, scores and agreement.</p></div></div></div></div></section>
